Bizarre Christmas Customs:

I read this weekend that in the 18th century, a favourite main course at
Christmas among the english aristocracy was roast cockatrice. This was made
by sewing together the back half of a small pig and the top half of a capon,
so I guess the mythical beast looked something like this !! (I believe a capon
is a castrated cockerel).

No mention in the article of anyone wielding this dish without gloves, or of
the effects of eating it ! 

